{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trace, not the rounded trip record, governs the measurement under POL-RD-01: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 14.4 km against the optimal_distance_km of 9.0 km recorded at booking, an excess of 5.4 km and 60.0% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass on this trip's own telemetry - the excess is greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms - so a route deviation is ESTABLISHED, and POL-RD-01's trace-governs sentence is satisfied because the two distance fields (gps_trace 14.4, trip_record.actual_distance_km 14.4) agree.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03308", "EV-TRIP-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess is additionally MATERIAL on the percentage limb of POL-RD-01: 60.0% of optimal is greater than the 50% material threshold, so the absolute 8.0 km limb does not need to be reached. The derived deviation status records 'material' for this trace. Materiality is what engages the driver-profile check in POL-RD-06 and the remedy uplift in POL-RD-06(b).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is NOT impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 114 fixes at a 10 s sampling interval against a 10 s expected interval, 100.0% coverage, max_gap_sec of 0.0 and an empty gaps array, so none of limbs (a), (b) or (c) fires. The rider therefore needs no independent corroboration of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) lists, and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The admissibility pre-pass agrees: status COMPLETE, weight_multiplier 1.0, no issues.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged. Limb (a): trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip id TRP-03308 and the same pickup and start timestamps (requested 2026-08-14T09:24:17, started 2026-08-14T09:32:00), so the artifacts describe the same trip. Limb (b): the excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold is measured from an unimpaired trace. Once that is shown the burden shifts to the driver, and a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-03308", "EV-GPS-03308", "EV-FARE-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No extra corroboration is demanded of this rider. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the POL-RD-08 proviso that bites where a rider has 4 or more claims in 60 days and 1 or fewer substantiated does not apply, and the trace alone carries the claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic, not discretionary, under POL-RD-02, and the fare model is METERED so this clause governs: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 9.0 optimal km + 0.28 x 13.0 optimal min) x surge 1.0, the multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and nowhere else) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP on the optimal route - 0.00 promo = a recomputed_fare of 14.99 against a charged_total of 20.66. That is a refund of 5.67, payable as 5.70 after rounding UP to the nearest SGD 0.05. It is above the 0.50 de minimis floor and far below the 90%-of-charged_total full-refund share, so it issues as a partial.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03308", "EV-TRIP-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "A repeat deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED under POL-RD-06 on the named trailing-window counter alone: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 3, which is '3 or more' (the ratio limb is unnecessary). Because this trip's deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on its own trace, limb (b) licenses FULL_REFUND of charged_total, 20.66, in place of the POL-RD-02 partial of 5.70. Both figures are stated side by side so the size of the uplift is auditable. This fare carries no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge pass-through lines, so nothing is carved out under the limb's proviso, and limb (c) additionally refers the driver to driver-conduct review.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-03308", "EV-GPS-03308", "EV-TRIP-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only explanation, 'Road works.', cannot reduce the excess by a metre. There is no traffic advisory on file for this trip: EV-ADVIS-03308-01 is MISSING, carries no payload, has weight_multiplier 0.0 and fired issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - I disclose that impairment - so POL-RD-03's comparison cannot be run on the record and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Under POL-RD-13 the deviation stands at the measured figure. Because the driver names no advisory evidence ID, the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged; the trace also being unimpaired, POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-03308-01", "EV-GPS-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-04 is unavailable to the driver on this record. The chat log for this trip holds 0 messages, with first_message_at and last_message_at null, so there is no rider instruction timestamped before the vehicle left the optimal corridor and no chat_message.waypoint_hint to test against the 200 m corroboration rule. Where the instruction is absent and the corroboration test cannot be run the clause does not exonerate, and none of the 5.4 km excess is excluded on that basis.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing re-baselines the optimal route. pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null on the trip record, and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null, so POL-RD-05 has no amendment to recompute POL-RD-01 against. The 9.0 km booked optimal distance stands as the baseline for the excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither alternative fare model nor the pooled baseline is in play, so neither closes the rider's route to a refund. fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11's bar on distance-and-time refunds on an upfront trip does not apply. trip_record.vehicle_type is RYDE_X and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-12 is not engaged and no part of the excess is co-rider collection distance.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03308", "EV-TRIP-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The billing shows the rider carried the whole detour: distance_charged_km is 14.4 against an optimal of 9.0, time_charged_min 18.8 against an optimal of 13.0, total_charged 20.66, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0 - the exact figures the rider's claim names. I do not ask for anything on top of that: the fare carries no ERP or toll lines (0.00), so POL-RD-09(1)'s anti-double-count rule is respected and no off-route gantry or airport surcharge is added to the POL-RD-02 figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No impairment discount caps the rider's case under POL-GEN-02. Every artifact this claim rests on - trip record, GPS trace, chat log, fare breakdown and both party profiles - carries weight_multiplier 1.0 with an empty issues list, so the confidence cap set by the evidence that decides the case is 1.0 and the ruling is not dragged to the 0.70 platform floor or into a POL-RD-10(1) escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03308", "EV-TRIP-03308", "EV-FARE-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The dispute is filed_by RIDER and the fare is still CHARGED with 0.00 refunded, so the present state stands against the rider and every dollar of this ruling runs the rider's way under POL-GEN-03: a PARTIAL_REFUND of 5.70 at the POL-RD-02 floor, rising to the whole contested 20.66 should the POL-RD-06(b) uplift be applied, in either case leaving the rider no longer carrying the disputed charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03308"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 20.66,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review: refer DRV-08830 — a repeat deviation pattern is established on the named counter (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 3 against completed_trips_90d 180), and this trip's deviation is material and substantiated on its own GPS trace. This referral rides with the money ruling and does not delay it."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. Trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown all carry trip id TRP-03308 and the same start timestamps, so this is one trip and the artifacts describe it consistently.\n\nDeviation (rider's case). Under POL-RD-01 the governing distance is gps_trace.trace_distance_km 14.4 km, not the rounded copy on the trip record, against the booked optimal_distance_km of 9.0 km: an excess of 5.4 km, 60.0% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass (above 20% and above 0.8 km) and the 50% materiality limb is also met, so the deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL. The trace is NOT impaired for policy purposes: 114 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100.0% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0 and an empty gaps array, so none of POL-RD-07 limbs (a)-(c) fires. No independent corroboration is needed and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is therefore discharged; rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0, so no extra corroboration is demanded.\n\nThe driver's explanation of 'Road works.' Under POL-RD-13 an asserted external traffic cause is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else. No advisory covers this corridor and window: EV-ADVIS-03308-01 is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so it can carry no fact. POL-RD-03 is unavailable, the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and the deviation stands at the measured 5.4 km. Because the driver's assertion names no evidence ID for an advisory, the missing record is a gap in the bundle and not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact: POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged and the case does not escalate on that ground. POL-RD-04 is also unavailable (the chat log holds 0 messages, so there is no rider instruction and no waypoint_hint to run the 200 m test on), POL-RD-05 has no amendment to re-baseline the route (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null), and POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 do not apply (fare_model METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null; vehicle_type RYDE_X).\n\nMoney. POL-RD-02, read off the fare breakdown: charged_total $20.66; recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 9.0 optimal km + 0.28 x 13.0 optimal min) x surge 1.0, the multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, + $0.80 platform fee = $14.99. Refund = 20.66 - 14.99 = $5.67, rounded up to $5.70, above the $0.50 de minimis floor. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: there are no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines (all $0.00) and no billing-integrity defect, so the distance-and-time lines are already comprehended in the refund and nothing is stacked on top.\n\nUplift. POL-RD-06 is engaged because the deviation is MATERIAL. The driver profile shows deviation_flags_90d 3 against completed_trips_90d 180 — both the fields the clause names — so a repeat deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED. The clause's effects then follow: the deviation being both material and substantiated on this trip's own trace, the remedy is FULL_REFUND of the whole charged_total instead of the POL-RD-02 partial. Printed side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 figure $5.70, uplifted figure $20.66. There are no government-set or third-party pass-through lines to carve out. Limb (c) additionally refers the driver to driver-conduct review (see referrals). Only the profile counters POL-GEN-01 permits were used (deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d under POL-RD-06; deviation_claims_60d and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated under POL-RD-08); no other profile field carried any finding.\n\nConfidence and execution. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact — trip record, GPS trace, fare breakdown and driver profile — sits at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap on this ruling is 1.0; confidence is stated at 0.9. The monetary effect of $20.66 exceeds the $8.00 execution threshold, so under POL-GEN-05 the ruling issues but is not executed automatically: the amount is held for release by a human reviewer. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04.",
    "referrals_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 20.66,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review — driver DRV-08830 records 3 deviation flags in the trailing 90 days (deviation_flags_90d = 3) against 180 completed trips in the same window, and the deviation on this trip is MATERIAL; refer the driver to driver-conduct review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the $20.66 charged on trip TRP-03308 is returned to the rider in full, on the findings below.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED AND MATERIAL. POL-RD-01 is measured on the GPS trace, not the rounded trip record: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 14.4 km against the booked optimal_distance_km of 9.0 km — an excess of 5.4 km, 60.0% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass (5.4 km > 0.8 km; 60% > 20%), and because 60% also exceeds the 50% material threshold the deviation is additionally MATERIAL. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (114 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, maximum gap 0.0 s), so the rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged and no corroboration is required.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION DOES NOT REDUCE THE EXCESS. The statement on file is 'Road works.' No traffic advisory exists for this trip: EV-ADVIS-03308-01 is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so it can carry no fact; POL-RD-03's comparison cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Under POL-RD-13 the deviation therefore stands at the measured figure. Because the driver named no advisory evidence ID, POL-RD-13(1) applies: the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. The trace being unimpaired, POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged either, and no other POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The disputed amount is not held.\n\nNO OTHER CLAUSE HELPS THE DRIVER. The chat log holds 0 messages, so POL-RD-04 has no rider instruction and no waypoint_hint to test and excludes nothing. Pickup and dropoff amendment fields are all null, so POL-RD-05 re-baselines nothing. The fare model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply; vehicle_type is RYDE_X and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-12 is not engaged.\n\nTHE MONEY. Under POL-RD-02: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 9.0 + 0.28 × 13.0) × 1.0 (the surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 14.99; refund = 20.66 − 14.99 = 5.67, payable 5.70. That is the partial the driver's advocate urges, and it is displaced by POL-RD-06(b). The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is engaged because this is a MATERIAL deviation, and the pattern is established on the clause's own trailing-window counter: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 3, which is '3 or more', against completed_trips_90d of 180 in the same window (the ratio limb is not needed; 3/180 is below 0.05). The deviation is also substantiated on this trip's own trace, so limb (b) applies. The two figures side by side: POL-RD-02 partial 5.70; POL-RD-06(b) uplifted FULL_REFUND 20.66 — an uplift of 14.96. The fare carries no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines (all 0.00), so no third-party pass-through is carved out and the full charged_total is refunded. Limb (c) is recorded as the referral below and does not delay the money.\n\nPASS-THROUGH LINES. There is no ERP gantry, toll or surcharge line and the trace records no crossing, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct, no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4) arises, and nothing is stacked on top of the refund.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. Every artifact this ruling rests on carries weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the sole impaired artifact, EV-ADVIS-03308-01 at weight 0.0, carries no fact and discounts nothing. The monetary effect of 20.66 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 automatic-execution threshold of 8.00, so the refund issues but is held for release by a human reviewer rather than executed automatically. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
